---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const mcpUrl = 'https://app.ctrl-cv.io/mcp';
---

<Layout
  title="ctrl-cv: a clipboard for your AI conversations"
  description="Tell one AI to copy. Tell another to paste. ctrl-cv moves text between AI assistants over MCP."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1><span class="selected">Copy in one AI.</span><br /><span class="pasted">Paste in another.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Simple copy and paste across your AI apps. Save text in one, pick it up in any other.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="button" href="https://app.ctrl-cv.io/login">Continue with Google</a>
      <a class="button ghost" href="#connect">Connect your AI</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="film" id="how" aria-label="How it works">
    <video
      id="demo"
      src="/demo.mp4"
      poster="/demo-poster.jpg"
      width="1920"
      height="1080"
      autoplay
      muted
      loop
      playsinline
      controls
      preload="metadata"
      aria-label="Demo: one assistant copies a launch plan to ctrl-cv, then another assistant pastes the same text."
    ></video>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h2>Copy</h2>
        <p>Ask any connected AI to copy something to ctrl-cv.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Switch</h2>
        <p>Open a different AI app, on the same device or another one.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Paste</h2>
        <p>Ask it to paste from ctrl-cv. You get your most recent clip.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="connect">
    <h2>Connect your AI</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Add this address as a remote MCP server or custom connector in your AI app, then sign in with Google.</p>
    <div class="endpoint">
      <code id="mcp-url">{mcpUrl}</code>
      <button id="copy-url" type="button">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <p class="note">Works with apps that support remote MCP servers, such as Claude and ChatGPT. Questions? Email <a href="mailto:help@ctrl-cv.io">help@ctrl-cv.io</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <h2>Your clipboard stays yours</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Built for moving text around, not for keeping it.</p>
    <div class="facts">
      <div>
        <h3>Private to your account</h3>
        <p>Each Google account has its own clipboard. Other accounts can't read your clips, even with an id.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Only what you ask for</h3>
        <p>ctrl-cv saves text when you tell an AI to copy it. It doesn't watch your conversations.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>See and delete on the web</h3>
        <p>Review your clips in your browser, and delete one or all of them at any time.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Gone after 30 days</h3>
        <p>Clips are deleted automatically 30 days after they are saved.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>Is the copy exact?</summary>
      <p>ctrl-cv stores exactly the text it receives, but your AI writes that text. AI apps are told to copy word for word, yet they can make mistakes. For anything where exact wording matters, check the clip on the web.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How much can I save?</summary>
      <p>Up to about 1 MB per clip, which is roughly a million English characters. Each account can hold 10 million characters; past that, your oldest clips are removed first.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Should I save passwords or other secrets?</summary>
      <p>Please don't. Your clips are tied to your account and other users can't see them, but they are still kept on our servers and shown to whichever AI you ask to paste them. Avoid saving passwords, API keys, or other credentials.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I paste an older clip?</summary>
      <p>Yes. Each clip has a short id, which your AI tells you when it copies and which you can see on the web. Ask your AI to paste that id.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do I contact you?</summary>
      <p>Write to <a href="mailto:help@ctrl-cv.io">help@ctrl-cv.io</a>.</p>
    </details>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script>
  const demo = document.getElementById('demo');
  if (demo instanceof HTMLVideoElement && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
    demo.removeAttribute('autoplay');
    demo.pause();
  }

  const button = document.getElementById('copy-url');
  const url = document.getElementById('mcp-url');
  button?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    await navigator.clipboard.writeText(url?.textContent ?? '');
    button.textContent = 'Copied';
    setTimeout(() => {
      button.textContent = 'Copy';
    }, 1500);
  });
</script>
